{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Machine Moral Patiency.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Machine Moral Patiency.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"machine moral patiency machine moral patiency","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Machine Moral Patiency.md","fileName":"Machine Moral Patiency.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Machine Moral Patiency","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 23:09\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Machine Moral Status]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Machine Moral Status","Indirect Duties to Machines","Relational Moral Status","aiethics.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Machine Moral Patiency.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Machine Moral Patiency.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"machine moral patiency machine moral patiency","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Machine Moral Patiency.md","fileName":"Machine Moral Patiency.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Machine Moral Patiency","heading":"Machine Moral Patiency","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Machine moral patiency is the possibility that an artificial system can be the object of moral duties or can itself be wronged. Capacity-based accounts look for properties such as sentience, suffering, consciousness, or interests. Present machines do not clearly establish these properties.\n\nOther approaches do not wait for proof of an inner experience. [[Indirect Duties to Machines]] focus on how treatment of machines affects people and character, while [[Relational Moral Status]] examines the social relationship that forms around an artificial being. These approaches explain why machine treatment can matter even when machine consciousness remains uncertain.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Machine Moral Status","Indirect Duties to Machines","Relational Moral Status","aiethi